WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.120
The trailer for Olaf's Frozen Adventure just
dropped and gives us a cool sneak peek at

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.550
the new Disney animated mini-movie starring
Frozen's snowman.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.530
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and I'm excited to see that while we wait

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.360
for Frozen 2, Disney will be treating us to
a 21-minute short film or featurette that

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.680
brings back for a holiday special all our
favourite Frozen characters including Elsa,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.560
Anna, Kristoff, Sven and Olaf.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.970
So, in this video, I'm going to be analysing
the new trailer and revealing some cool Frozen

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.000
and Disney easter eggs plus some other little
details you might have missed.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.629
When the Frozen filmmaking team began dreaming
up stories for the first Frozen-themed short

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:41.519
film, Frozen Fever, many of their initial
ideas actually focused on Olaf the snowman!

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:45.820
Of course, in the end, they turned their attention
to Elsa and Anna instead, but, as is clear

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.159
from the title and trailer for Olaf's Frozen
Adventure, the filmmaking team have decided

00:00:50.159 --> 00:00:54.530
to put the friendly snowman very much at the
front-and-centre of their storytelling again!

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.170
Speaking of Frozen Fever, there are some nice
little parallels between that short and this

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.170
new one.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.730
For example, both stories centre on family
celebrations and traditions, with Frozen Fever

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:10.060
being all about birthday festivities while
Olaf's Frozen Adventure is all about the holiday

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.490
season; in fact, in this new short film, Elsa
and her sister will be celebrating this particular

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.479
holiday for the first time since they were
reunited.

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:22.299
Also, both short films feature characters
on the hunt for something around Arendelle:

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:27.299
in Frozen Fever, Elsa sent her sister on a
scavenger hunt for birthday gifts, while this

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.680
new film sees Olaf on the hunt for holiday
traditions so he can celebrate the season

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.679
with Elsa and her sister who were apart so
long that they don't have any family traditions

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:36.910
of their own.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.909
By the way, on the subject of family, the
family portrait we see in the trailer is actually

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:44.340
an original piece of concept art for the movie
Frozen.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.479
During Olaf's adventure, we see him enjoying
finding out about the different ways families

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:49.950
mark the holidays.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.939
And there's a very funny easter egg for Wreck-It
Ralph when he grabs a candy cane and uses

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:57.270
it to replace his carrot nose, exclaiming
"Sugar Rush!"

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.009
In the first Wreck-It Ralph movie, Ralph enters
a go-kart racing candy-filled game called

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:06.240
Sugar Rush which features a Candy Cane Forest
where he meets Vanellope.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.670
Wreck-It-Ralph 2 is actually Disney's next
animated movie so it's cool that they added

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.820
a little nod to it here, as they also did
in Moana.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.950
There's a touch of adult humour in this moment
as well as the way Olaf's eyes spin reminded

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.170
me of the reaction of the main characters
in animated movies like Pinocchio and The

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:26.130
Good Dinosaur when they got rather different
rushes.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:29.900
One of the festive traditions that Olaf learns
about in the scene you can see here is the

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.340
feast of Saint Lucia, which in a number of
Nordic countries, like the ones that inspired

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:39.920
the Frozen movies, is celebrated on 13th December,
and includes a girl typically wearing a white

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.170
gown and red sash together with a wreath of
candles on her head.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.710
And, as you can see from his sleigh, Olaf
collects quite a few gifts on his travels

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:48.710
with Sven.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.530
And hidden in this shot of the sleigh, there's
a green toy with a little tuft of reddish-pink

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.310
hair which could be a nod to Elliot from Pete's
Dragon.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.830
And you can also just make out what looks
like a Troll, which is call-back to the Trolls

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:06.110
in the original Frozen movie and the Troll
statues outside Oaken's store.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:10.481
And it looks like Olaf will be paying a visit
to Oaken's sauna in this short film too, which

00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:14.590
makes sense as, although it's a different
season here, we know from Olaf's 'In Summer'

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.970
song that he likes the idea of 'lettin' off
steam'!

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.480
In fact, Olaf's Frozen Adventure doesn't just
link very nicely back to Disney's previous

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.000
Frozen tales, but, according to John Lasseter,
who's Chief Creative Officer at Disney and

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.180
Pixar Animation Studios, it also "fits in
perfectly with Frozen 2", which is due out

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.320
in cinemas in November 2019.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.510
Indeed, as Lasseter told EW, 'you could sit
down and watch Olaf's Frozen Adventure and

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.770
Frozen 2 as one big marathon.'

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:46.030
Which makes it sound like this latest tale
really is part of the building blocks for

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:50.850
the much-anticipated Frozen sequel, which
will follow the lives of Elsa and her sister

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.400
after the events of this new short.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.890
Of course, one of the mega-popular parts of
the Frozen movies are their insanely catchy

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.890
songs.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:02.530
For Frozen and Frozen Fever, those tunes were
written by husband-and-wife team Robert Lopez

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.540
and Kristen Anderson-Lopez.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.780
This time though, there's a new song-writing
duo in the kingdom: Kate Anderson and Elyssa

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.570
Samsel, and they've written four original
songs for the new mini-movie.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.709
And, in case you're wondering, the track you
hear in the trailer is called 'When We're

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:21.150
Together', and notice how, as the sisters
sing the song, Elsa seems to be sending Olaf

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:25.500
up into the air with a star that has a mini-snowman
figure frozen inside it.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.800
And did Olaf put the same star on top of the
Christmas tree here?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.510
By the way, the look of the tree and the snowflake
shape underneath makes me think that Elsa

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:38.610
has fashioned this tree herself out of ice,
in a similar way to how she made an ice sculpture

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.280
for her sister's birthday in Frozen Fever.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:46.110
Although Olaf's Frozen Adventure was initially
going to make its debut on TV, now it's going

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:51.000
to premiere on the big screen in front of
Pixar's animated movie, Coco, in a similar

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.410
way to how the short film Frozen Fever first
screened in front of Disney's live-action

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.410
movie Cinderella.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.760
And it's interesting that both Olaf's Frozen
Adventure and Coco share a common theme of

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:05.840
family traditions centred around big celebrations,
with Olaf's Adventure focusing on the December

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.790
holidays and Coco on the Day of the Dead.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.810
By the way, to find out lots more about Coco,
hit the top-right of the screen to watch my

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.760
video on Pixar's new movie.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.220
Now, how excited are you for Olaf's Frozen
Adventure?

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.930
And what would you like to see happen in Frozen
2?

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.110
Let me know in the comments below!

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.080
And if you enjoyed this, do please hit that
like button and tap the screen to check out

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.440
more of my other Disney animation videos,
including cool facts you might not know about

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.500
Frozen Fever.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.360
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.340
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

